\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 8.1Participants retain ownership of their bot code, subject to applicable third-party rights. They grant the Organizer, the Hosts, and their respective affiliates a nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to access, reproduce, execute, and evaluate submitted code solely to administer, support, troubleshoot, judge, and verify the Competition. They also grant those entities permission to reproduce, display, distribute, and use hand logs and anonymized results for Competition replays, publicity, judging, and post-event analysis. Participants must provide code and documentation reasonably requested by the Organizer to verify compliance. Submissions are provided without an obligation of confidentiality; participants must not submit materials they are not authorized to disclose. No ownership transfer or general-purpose license to commercialize participant code is required under these rules.\
8.2The Organizer will collect and use registration data to administer the event as described in the privacy notice made available during registration at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pokerbot.sequoiacap.com/privacy.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 pokerbot.sequoiacap.com/privacy.html}}. Registration data will be shared with event partners only if the participant separately opts in during registration. Any Host receiving participant data will process it in accordance with its applicable privacy notice, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 openai.com/policies/privacy-policy}} for OpenAI. Participation is not conditioned on consent to Host marketing or recruiting communications.\
8.3Participants acknowledge that photos and videos may be taken during the event and grant the Organizer and Hosts (Sequoia Capital Operations, LLC, OpenAI, and Citadel Securities) and their affiliates the sublicensable right to use those photos and videos in internal and external marketing and promotional materials, unless they notify the Organizer and Hosts that they wish to opt out. The Organizer will provide a clearly identified contact and a reasonable process for making and implementing a photo and video opt-out before recording begins. Participants also permit the Organizer and Hosts to publish their names, team names, rankings, and results in connection with the Competition and its publicity, without additional compensation, except where prohibited by law.\
8.4Each participant represents and warrants that they have all rights, licenses, consents, and permissions necessary to submit their code and other materials, participate in the Competition, and grant the rights in these rules. Submissions and the uses authorized by these rules must not infringe third-party intellectual property, privacy, publicity, or other rights, breach confidentiality obligations, or violate applicable law. Participants must comply with applicable third-party software and data licenses. Submissions must not contain personal information, third-party confidential information, malware, hardcoded credentials, plaintext passwords, or code designed to compromise the platform or other submissions.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

