9.4To the maximum extent permitted by law, participants release the Competition Entities from claims arising from technical malfunctions, unavailable services, lost or incorrectly processed submissions, errors in scoring or prize announcements, and participation in the Competition or use of a prize. Competition materials and the competition platform are provided as available and without warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or noninfringement. Participants are responsible for their own equipment, expenses, and review and testing of code. No release or disclaimer applies to gross negligence, willful misconduct, or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.\
9.5To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Competition Entities will not be liable under these rules for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, including lost profits or lost opportunities. Each Host's aggregate liability arising out of the Competition or these rules will not exceed US$100. These limitations do not apply to fraud, gross negligence, willful misconduct, or liability that cannot lawfully be limited. Claims concerning use of OpenAI services remain governed by the applicable OpenAI agreement, including its warranties, disclaimers, limitations of liability, and dispute-resolution provisions.\
